# Vendored protocol definitions. They are not merely build inputs: the package
# installs native/mwl.c, mwl.h, build.sh and these XMLs under
# /usr/lib/matrix-overlay/native/ so that a user (or this package) can rebuild
# the layer-shell client when the prebuilt library does not work on their
# compositor, and mwl.sources_digest() hashes the XMLs to detect a stale build.
# wlr-layer-shell-unstable-v1 is not distributed by wayland-protocols at all, so
# vendoring it is the only way to build against it without dragging in wlroots.
# The two others do exist in wayland-protocols, but switching to the distro copy
# would break that tested rebuild path or make it a runtime dependency.
# Provenance, so a reviewer can compare bytes without guessing:
Files: native/wlr-layer-shell-unstable-v1.xml
Copyright: 2017 Drew DeVault
License: X11
Comment: from wlroots protocol/wlr-layer-shell-unstable-v1.xml; interface
 zwlr_layer_shell_v1 version 5; sha256
 87e0b9c837aecd6977f76f3c47d73088b7159871f5d979dc1840f6cadb5e2ed8. This is the
 no-endorsement variant of the MIT/X11 text, not the plain Expat text, so it is
 licensed under its own name rather than lumped in with the others.

Files: native/xdg-output-unstable-v1.xml
Copyright: 2017 Red Hat Inc.
License: MIT
Comment: from wayland-protocols unstable/xdg-output/xdg-output-unstable-v1.xml;
 interface zxdg_output_v1 version 3; sha256
 e20aa6f87bd8cc473b7ee1175604e2e09ce8227eadadc55ad8e3f9d003c251a3

Files: native/xdg-shell.xml
Copyright: 2008-2013 Kristian Høgsberg
 2013-2016 Rafael Antognolli, Jasper St. Pierre and the Wayland contributors
License: MIT
Comment: from wayland-protocols stable/xdg-shell/xdg-shell.xml; interface
 xdg_wm_base version 7; sha256
 9d9e27038ca722f159a361293f8c6cd270dab907ab52de5b8ecfbb8d6b9651c2. It is linked
 in by native/build.sh because the generated layer-shell code references
 xdg_popup_interface, not because this client maps windows.

